---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { website, person } from "../lib/jsonld";

const roles = await getCollection("roles");
// Newest first by start year; an open-ended engagement wins a tie.
const startYear = (period: string) => Number(period.match(/\d{4}/)?.[0] ?? 0);
const ongoing = (period: string) => /ongoing|since/.test(period);
const references = (await getCollection("references")).sort(
  (a, b) =>
    startYear(b.data.period) - startYear(a.data.period) ||
    Number(ongoing(b.data.period)) - Number(ongoing(a.data.period)),
);
const description = "What Steffen Rörtgen can be hired for: Nostr protocol-based systems, metadata infrastructure for education, SKOS vocabularies and linked data, workshops and consulting. What he brings, and who he has worked for.";
---
<Base title={`Work · ${site.name}`} description={description} path="/work/" jsonLd={[website(), person()]}>
  <h2 class="section-title">Work</h2>
  <p>I build the plumbing that makes open education findable. Things I can be hired for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nostr protocol-based systems</strong>: relays, crawlers, indexes, and clients that avoid platform lock-in.</li>
    <li><strong>Metadata infrastructure for education</strong>: data models, application profiles, validation, and the pipelines around them.</li>
    <li><strong>SKOS vocabularies and linked data</strong>: publishing, reconciliation, and setting up <a href="https://skohub.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkoHub</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Workshops and consulting</strong>: standards selection, metadata strategy, and hands-on training for editorial and developer teams.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 class="section-title" data-en="What I bring" data-de="Was ich mitbringe">What I bring</h2>
    <div class="lang-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Language of this section">
      <button type="button" data-lang="en" aria-pressed="true">EN</button>
      <button type="button" data-lang="de" aria-pressed="false">DE</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="lang-block" lang="en" data-lang="en">
    <li><strong>Ideas that get tested in public.</strong> In 2025 I wrote <a href="/articles/h-k72fOoZmf_SOC3cUpqc-en/">an essay</a> arguing that open education needs a shared protocol rather than more platforms. Since then a small group of us has been building exactly that on Nostr: the <a href="https://edufeed.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">edufeed</a> relays now hold over 100,000 AMB-described resources, a <a href="https://comcal.edufeed.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">community calendar</a>, and an <a href="https://gitworkshop.dev/laoc.xyz/amb-mcp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCP server</a> for AI assistants. The <a href="/articles/u-FPi10MVJ5GHRkGdis0X/">2026 status report</a> describes what works and what does not yet.</li>
    <li><strong>Standards work, not only standards use.</strong> I have been part of the DINI-AG-KIM metadata groups since the <a href="https://w3id.org/kim/amb/latest/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AMB</a> profile was taking shape, and I led its curricula group until the MEM project was set up at FWU to pursue that work in a dedicated way. I wrote the <a href="https://git.edufeed.org/edufeed/nips" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NIP-AMB, NIP-VOCAB, and NIP-DIDACTIC</a> specifications that carry AMB and SKOS over Nostr. In 2024 the BMBF appointed me to its OER advisory board for metadata infrastructure. I have published <a href="https://doi.org/10.18420/delfi2023-24" target="_blank" rel="noopener">evaluation criteria</a> for choosing metadata standards, and the <a href="https://www.pedocs.de/frontdoor.php?source_opus=29235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kompendium Didaktische Metadaten</a>, written together with Manuel Oellers, collects what we know about metadata and education infrastructure in one place.</li>
    <li><strong>Software</strong> <a href="https://skohub.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkoHub</a>, which I maintained at hbz, runs at IQB, SODIX/FWU, and WirLernenOnline. The prototype I built at GWDG became the basis of the <a href="https://wirlernenonline.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WirLernenOnline</a> ETL pipeline and search. Curricula as linked data started as a <a href="/projects/frameworks-as-linked-data/">side project in 2020</a> and led to a project at FWU that is developing the <a href="https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">machine-readable curricula ontology</a> further.</li>
    <li><strong>Protocols over platforms, with open eyes.</strong> I have built on ActivityPub and on Nostr (edufeed), and tried <a href="/posts/2023-06-30/">RDF on both</a>. What I care about is that data and identities stay portable and that public education infrastructure does not walk into lock-in and silo traps.</li>
  </ul>
  <ul class="lang-block" lang="de" data-lang="de" hidden>
    <li><strong>Ideen, die öffentlich erprobt werden.</strong> 2025 habe ich in <a href="/articles/h-k72fOoZmf_SOC3cUpqc/">einem Essay</a> argumentiert, dass offene Bildung ein gemeinsames Protokoll braucht und nicht noch mehr Plattformen. Seitdem baut eine kleine Gruppe von uns genau das auf Nostr: Auf den <a href="https://edufeed.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">edufeed</a>-Relays liegen inzwischen über 100.000 mit AMB beschriebene Ressourcen, ein <a href="https://comcal.edufeed.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Community-Kalender</a> und ein <a href="https://gitworkshop.dev/laoc.xyz/amb-mcp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCP-Server</a> für KI-Assistenten. Der <a href="/articles/u-FPi10MVJ5GHRkGdis0X/">Zwischenbericht von 2026</a> beschreibt, was funktioniert und was noch nicht.</li>
    <li><strong>Standards mitgestalten, nicht nur anwenden.</strong> Ich bin in den Metadaten-Gruppen der DINI-AG-KIM dabei, seit das <a href="https://w3id.org/kim/amb/latest/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AMB</a>-Profil Gestalt angenommen hat, und habe dort die Curricula-Gruppe geleitet, bis das MEM-Projekt eingerichtet wurde, um das Vorhaben dediziert zu begleiten. Ich habe die Spezifikationen <a href="https://git.edufeed.org/edufeed/nips" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NIP-AMB, NIP-VOCAB und NIP-DIDACTIC</a> geschrieben, die AMB und SKOS über Nostr transportieren. 2024 hat mich das BMBF für Metadateninfrastruktur in seinen OER-Beirat berufen. Zur Auswahl von Metadatenstandards habe ich <a href="https://doi.org/10.18420/delfi2023-24" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bewertungskriterien</a> publiziert. In dem <a href="https://www.pedocs.de/frontdoor.php?source_opus=29235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kompendium Didaktische Metadaten</a>, welches ich gemeinsam mit Manuel Oellers verfasst habe, sind umfangreiche Informationen rund um Metadaten und Bildungsinfrastrukturen zusammengefasst.</li>
    <li><strong>Software</strong> <a href="https://skohub.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkoHub</a>, das ich am hbz betreut habe, läuft bei IQB, SODIX/FWU und WirLernenOnline. Der Prototyp, den ich an der GWDG gebaut habe, wurde zur Grundlage der ETL-Pipeline und Suche von <a href="https://wirlernenonline.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WirLernenOnline</a>. Lehrpläne als Linked Data begannen 2020 als <a href="/projects/frameworks-as-linked-data/">Nebenprojekt</a> und sind in einem Projekt gemündet, das die <a href="https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ontologie für maschinenlesbare Lehrpläne</a> am FWU weiterentwickelt.</li>
    <li><strong>Protokolle statt Plattformen, mit offenen Augen.</strong> Ich habe Erfahrungen mit ActivityPub und Nostr (edufeed) gebaut und <a href="/posts/2023-06-30/">RDF auf beidem</a> ausprobiert. Mir geht es darum, dass Daten und Identitäten portabel bleiben und öffentliche Bildungsinfrastruktur in keine Lock-In und Silo-Fallen läuft.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-title">Clients and references</h2>
  <ul>
    {references.map((r) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{r.data.url ? <a href={r.data.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{r.data.org}</a> : r.data.org}</strong>
        <span class="meta"> · {r.data.period}</span><br />
        {r.data.work}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-title">Committees</h2>
  <ul>{roles.map((r) => <li>{r.data.body}{r.data.since && ` (since ${r.data.since})`}</li>)}</ul>

  <script>
    const KEY = "work-lang";
    const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".lang-toggle button");
    const blocks = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".lang-block");
    const title = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".section-head .section-title");
    const apply = (lang: string) => {
      blocks.forEach((b) => (b.hidden = b.dataset.lang !== lang));
      buttons.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b.dataset.lang === lang)));
      if (title) title.textContent = title.dataset[lang] ?? title.textContent;
    };
    let saved: string | null = null;
    try { saved = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch {}
    if (saved === "de") apply("de");
    buttons.forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const lang = b.dataset.lang ?? "en";
        apply(lang);
        try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, lang); } catch {}
      }),
    );
  </script>
</Base>
